---
title: Confirm Your Generated Output
---

This Codespace doesn't have Xcode or macOS available, so you can't build, run, or open the iOS app to see your changes visually. Instead, "verification" in this tutorial means confirming that each Generator_Script printed a success message and that the generated files it wrote actually contain the values you edited.

## Check Your Work

{% steps %}

1. Scroll back through your terminal history for each of the three generator scripts you ran (`generateEnvironmentConstants.sh`, `generate-app-config.py`, and `generate-app-theme.py`) and confirm each one printed a `✅` success line, not a `❌` error line.

2. Open `VERAConfiguration/VERAConfiguration/AppConfig.swift` and confirm it contains the flag value(s) you edited in Step 04 (for example, the updated `allowScreenShare` or `defaultLayoutMode` values).

3. Open `VERAApp/VERA/App/Generated/EnvironmentConstants.swift` and confirm it contains the `BASE_API_URL` you exported in Step 02.

4. List the contents of `VERACommonUI/VERACommonUI/Resources/SemanticColors.xcassets/` and open the edited token's `<name>.colorset/Contents.json` (for example, `primary.colorset/Contents.json`) to confirm the updated RGBA components from Step 06 appear.

{% /steps %}

{% aside %}
This tutorial does not build, run, or open the app in Xcode, an iOS Simulator, or a physical device. No browser-based verification is required either — everything you just checked lives in your terminal history and in the generated files themselves.
{% /aside %}

Next, you'll wrap up and see where to go from here.
